{%- comment -%}
  THE OASIS — category tabs from plain text

  The menu-driven tab list needs a navigation menu and, for filtering, tagged
  products. On a page template neither is available, so this variant takes a
  typed list instead — one tab per line, "Label | /url".

  A line with no URL renders as plain text rather than a dead link, so the row
  can be filled in with labels now and pointed somewhere later. If no tab
  matches the current URL, the first one is shown as active, which is what the
  design shows on the unfiltered page.

  FILTER MODE (filter_tags: true, collection routes only)
  Each tab filters the collection it already sits in, rather than linking away.
  The first row is always the "show everything" tab. After that, the text
  following the pipe is read as:
    - a whole filter query when it contains "=", e.g. filter.v.availability=0
    - otherwise a product tag, e.g. Floral
  and an empty value means the tag is spelled exactly like the label. The row is
  wrapped in <oasis-tab-filter>, which swaps the grid in place rather than
  loading a page.

  A filter only works if Shopify knows about it: a tag tab needs a Product tag
  filter added in Search & Discovery, or Shopify ignores the parameter and hands
  back the unfiltered collection.

  The links stay real hrefs so that a middle-click still opens the filtered
  collection in a new tab, and so the row works with JavaScript off.

  Accepts:
    - links: {String} one per line, "Label | /url" (url optional)
    - aria_label: {String}
    - filter_tags: {Boolean} turn on filter mode
    - results: {Object} the collection, for reading which tag is active
    - results_url: {String} the collection's own URL, for the "all" tab
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if links != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign rows = links | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'

    comment
      Every filter currently applied, as an encoded "|param=value|" list, so a
      tab can test for its own query with a single contains. Encoded because
      that is the form the tabs carry, and the two have to compare like for like.
    endcomment
    assign active_params = '|'
    if filter_tags and results != blank
      for oasis_filter in results.filters
        for oasis_value in oasis_filter.active_values
          assign oasis_encoded = oasis_value.value | url_encode
          assign active_params = active_params | append: oasis_filter.param_name | append: '=' | append: oasis_encoded | append: '|'
        endfor
      endfor
    endif

    comment
      Link mode only: work out the active tab first, so "no match" can fall back
      to the first.
    endcomment
    assign active_index = 0
    for row in rows
      assign parts = row | split: '|'
      assign row_label = parts[0] | strip
      assign row_href = parts[1] | strip
      if row_label != blank and row_href != blank
        assign row_path = row_href | split: '?' | first
        if row_path == request.path
          assign active_index = forloop.index
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    if active_index == 0
      assign active_index = 1
    endif
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Build the items first and emit nothing at all if none survive, so a setting
    that is nil or holds only separators can't leave an empty <nav> behind.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture tab_items -%}
      {%- for row in rows -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign parts = row | split: '|'
          assign row_label = parts[0] | strip
          assign row_value = parts[1] | strip

          if filter_tags
            comment
              The first row clears every filter; the rest carry a query. A value
              holding "=" is used as written, so a tab can filter on anything
              Shopify offers; anything else is treated as a product tag.
            endcomment
            if forloop.first
              assign row_query = ''
              assign row_href = results_url
            else
              if row_value contains '='
                assign row_query = row_value
              else
                assign row_tag = row_value | default: row_label
                assign row_tag_enc = row_tag | url_encode
                assign row_query = 'filter.p.tag=' | append: row_tag_enc
              endif
              assign row_href = results_url | append: '?' | append: row_query
            endif

            assign is_active = false
            if row_query == blank
              if active_params == '|'
                assign is_active = true
              endif
            else
              assign row_probe = '|' | append: row_query | append: '|'
              if active_params contains row_probe
                assign is_active = true
              endif
            endif
          else
            assign row_query = ''
            assign row_href = row_value
            assign is_active = false
            if forloop.index == active_index
              assign is_active = true
            endif
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if row_label != blank -%}
          <li class="oasis-tabs__item">
            {%- if row_href != blank -%}
              <a
                class="oasis-tabs__link{% if is_active %} oasis-tabs__link--active{% endif %}"
                href="{{ row_href | escape }}"
                {% if filter_tags %}
                  data-oasis-filter="{{ row_query | escape }}"
                {% endif %}
                {% if is_active %}
                  aria-current="page"
                {% endif %}
              >
                {{- row_label | escape -}}
              </a>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="oasis-tabs__link{% if is_active %} oasis-tabs__link--active{% endif %}">
                {{- row_label | escape -}}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- if tab_items != blank -%}
    {%- if filter_tags -%}<oasis-tab-filter>{%- endif -%}
      <nav class="oasis-tabs__nav" aria-label="{{ aria_label | default: 'Product categories' | escape }}">
        <ul class="oasis-tabs__list">{{ tab_items }}</ul>
      </nav>
    {%- if filter_tags -%}</oasis-tab-filter>{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
